{"metadata":{"name":"Sunan an Nasai","section":{"1":{"eng-name":"The Book of Purification","ara-name":"كتاب الطهارة"}},"section_detail":{"1":{"hadithnumber_first":1,"hadithnumber_last":324,"arabicnumber_first":1,"arabicnumber_last":324}}},"hadiths":[{"hadithnumber":104,"arabicnumber":104,"text":"Rapporté par Bilal : J'ai vu le Prophète (ﷺ) passer ses mains mouillées sur les Khuffs et le Khimar.* *Un couvre-chef qui ne se limite pas à l'usage courant du « turban », comme il ressort clairement du premier récit","grades":[{"name":"Abu Ghuddah","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih Muslim"}],"reference":{"book":1,"hadith":104},"chapter":{"id":86,"ara-name":"باب الْمَسْحِ عَلَى الْعِمَامَةِ ","eng-name":"Wiping Over The 'Imamah (Turban) [1]","isFirstHadith":true}}]}